  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.18,
      "text": " You've got your weapon. You've got your camp. But you can't survive alone. So you form a group,"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.54,
      "end": 10.32,
      "text": " your best friend, a nurse who knows first aid, and a mechanic who can fix anything."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.86,
      "end": 16.32,
      "text": " Four people. One goal. Survive. Day 1. You lock the school gates."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.28,
      "end": 24.34,
      "text": " Day 10. You've got rice, canned food, water, medicine, even a generator. For the first time."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.94,
      "end": 33.04,
      "text": " You feel safe. Day 20. A man knocks on the gate. He's hurt. He's hungry. He's begging for help."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.6,
      "end": 39.16,
      "text": " What would you do? You let him in. You give him food, water, a bed. He looks around,"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.48,
      "end": 44.46,
      "text": " counts your supplies. And the next morning, he's gone. Two nights later, headlights,"
    },
    {
      "start": 44.78,
      "end": 50.76,
      "text": " engines, tenon men at your gate. And he's standing in front of them. Because here's the truth. Zombies"
    },
    {
      "start": 50.76,
      "end": 58.86,
      "text": " only want your flesh. But humans want everything you have. Your food, your water, your weapons,"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.52,
      "end": 66.1,
      "text": " your camp. And so remember three rules. Rule 1. I never show strangers your supplies."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.6,
      "end": 73.72,
      "text": " Rule 2. Hide your stash in more than one place. Rule 3. Someone stays awake every single night."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.28,
      "end": 81.54,
      "text": " Zombies are slow and dumb. Humans think. Humans plan. And humans never stop."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.48,
      "end": 86.72,
      "text": " But here's the real question. What about the people inside your group? Can you really trust"
    },
    {
      "start": 86.72,
      "end": 90.1,
      "text": " them? Find out in part 4. Subscribe so you don't miss it."
    }
  ],
